+++ b/fontawesome-inert.css
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+/* Offline inert stand-in for the third-party icon webfont stylesheet the pristine entry document
+   pulled from a CDN (index.html:7, cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.2.1/css/all.min.css,
+   removed by the same adaptation face that adds this file). Added by the harness
+   (environment/adaptation.patch), not by the author.
+
+   What this file deliberately does NOT contain:
+     - no @font-face rule, so the browser has nothing to fetch: the served face makes zero requests
+       to any host other than the loopback address it is served from (measurable through
+       window.__RB_SEED_FACE__.blocked / .same_origin_only, installed by js/rb/seed.js);
+     - no downloaded or vendored glyph artwork, and no invented artwork either;
+     - no rule that changes the geometry, colour, stacking or hit testing of anything the
+       application styles itself. Every declaration below is confined to the icon slots.
+
+   What it does contain is only the box-metrics half of the upstream icon rules, so the five icon
+   slots in this tree keep their inline-box geometry, their line box and their direction and stay
+   exactly where the page puts them. The five slots (a tree-wide census, 0 other uses):
+     index.html:79  <i class="fa-solid fa-bars">            the Activities button glyph
+     index.html:89  <button id="close-menu" class="fa-regular fa-circle-xmark">   the menu close box
+     js/libs.js:135 <i class="fa-solid fa-mars|fa-venus">   the gender glyph in a relationship row
+     js/menu.js:1134 <i class="fa-brands fa-youtube">       the social-media row glyph
+     js/menu.js:1135 <i class="fa-brands fa-instagram">     the social-media row glyph
+   The font stack is 'inherit' on purpose: each slot keeps whatever text the document already put
+   there (which is none - all five are empty elements whose only content was the ligature the
+   webfont supplied), so nothing had to be drawn or downloaded to replace it. Font size is
+   inherited rather than pinned so a slot does not blow up to icon-glyph size.
+
+   Consequence for verification, stated so nobody asserts on it later: glyph shape, glyph identity
+   and font family are NOT observable on this face and no checkpoint reads them. A tree-wide search
+   found 0 places where application JavaScript reads a computed font family, a glyph metric, an
+   ::before content string or an icon bounding box, so the icon stylesheet is decorative at
+   runtime: it cannot change any value, any branch or any control flow. Every assertion in
+   tests/dsl.json reads text, a number, a boolean, an element count, an inline style the page sets
+   itself, a computed display the page's own stylesheet sets, or a scalar returned by the
+   read-only probe. */
+
+.fa,
+.fas,
+.far,
+.fab,
+.fa-solid,
+.fa-regular,
+.fa-brands {
+    font-family: inherit;
+    font-weight: normal;
+    font-style: normal;
+    font-size: inherit;
+    display: inline-block;
+    line-height: 1;
+    letter-spacing: normal;
+    text-transform: none;
+    white-space: nowrap;
+    word-wrap: normal;
+    direction: ltr;
+    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
+}
